# SWE3004 Operating Systems — Projects 0–3

Implementation of **xv6-riscv** projects for the **SWE3004 Operating Systems** course.

## Projects

| Project | Topic | Main Concepts |
|---|---|---|
| **Project 0** | Booting xv6 | xv6, RISC-V, QEMU, OS boot process |
| **Project 1** | System Calls | System-call interface, process management, memory |
| **Project 2** | CPU Scheduling | EEVDF, nice values, virtual runtime, deadlines |
| **Project 3** | Virtual Memory | `mmap()`, page faults, `munmap()`, demand paging |

---

## Project 0 — Booting xv6

- Set up and booted **xv6-riscv** using QEMU.
- Modified the boot message to display personal information.
- Studied the basic boot process and structure of xv6.

**Key Concepts**
- xv6-riscv
- RISC-V
- QEMU
- OS boot process

---

## Project 1 — System Calls

Implemented and extended the xv6 system-call interface.

**Implemented System Calls**
- `getnice(int pid)`
- `setnice(int pid, int value)`
- `ps(int pid)`
- `uint64 meminfo(void)`
- `waitpid(int pid)`

**Key Concepts**
- User-level system-call interface
- `ecall`
- System-call dispatch
- Process management
- Memory information
- Process waiting

**System Call Flow**

```text
User Program
    ↓
user.h / usys.pl
    ↓
ecall
    ↓
syscall.c
    ↓
sysproc.c
    ↓
proc.c
